WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:03.837
-You know, it's difficult to
keep up with the number

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:06.572
of Trump aides and officials who
have been fired or forced out.

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:08.908
Many have moved on,
several are under indictment,

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:10.844
and some of those
we think have left

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:12.378
haven't really gone anywhere
at all.

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:15.515
For a look at where they are,
it's time for "The Check In."

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.149 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:18.884
[ Bell dings ]

00:00:18.884 --> 00:00:20.153
Throughout the campaign,

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:21.920
President Trump constantly
bragged about knowing

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.590
the best people, and then
promised to hire those people

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.493
once he got
into the White House.

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:28.762
-I know the best people.
I know the best managers.

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:30.763
I know the best dealmakers.

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:33.666
I know people
that will make us so strong.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:37.003
I know guys that are so good.

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.904
I put people in
that have great ability.

00:00:38.904 --> 00:00:41.174
But the cabinet, we're gonna
have all the best people.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:44.577
We got the smartest -- I know
the smartest, I know the best.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.212
I know the best negotiators.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.080
I know the ones
that are overrated.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.682
I know the ones
you never heard of

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:51.451
that are better
than all of them.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.619
But we're gonna use
our best people.

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:57.057
-You know what I don't think
you use? The best thesaurus.

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.658
[ Laughter ]
You use "best" so much,

00:00:59.658 --> 00:01:02.162
you're basically
President Kenny Bania.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.629
-I told you Mendy's
had the best pea soup.

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:05.731
The best, Jerry. The best.

00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:08.367
[ Laughter ]
-And when Trump wasn't...

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:11.137
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.172
And when Trump wasn't bragging
about how his people

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:17.009
were the best, he was bragging
about how awful they were.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:18.912
-I'm going to get these great
business leaders.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:20.980
I will get these
great business leaders.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.715
These great, great people.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:25.518
And I have to say some of them
are not nice people.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:28.688
Do you agree? Who cares? Right?
Who cares?

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.156
Some of them you don't want
to have dinner with.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.692
They are vicious, brutal,
horrible human beings.

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:34.327
Who cares? Who the hell cares?

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:37.597
Some are nice,
but some are terrible people.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.265
-Really?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:42.434
Really covering your bases
there.

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:43.903
[ Imitating Trump ]
"These people are the best

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:47.673
"and also the worst. We got
geniuses, business giants,

00:01:47.673 --> 00:01:50.743
also we got some murderers."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.845
"We got people who take their
shoes off on airplanes.

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:55.415
It's a mixed bag."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:56.616
[ Normal voice ] But I have to
give Trump credit here,

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:57.983
because he did warn us
that he was going to hire

00:01:57.983 --> 00:02:00.487
some vicious, horrible people,
and he followed through.

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:03.656
And then, as expected, some of
those awful people got fired

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:06.659
for their awfulness, but they
didn't exactly go away.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.428
Take former Navy SEAL
and surrogate

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.896
for the Trump campaign,
Carl Higbie.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:13.099
Higbie was appointed to be
the face of an agency called

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:15.901
the Corporation for National
&amp; Community Service.

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.437
His job was to...

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.012
Basically, he was doing PR
for people who help people.

00:02:27.012 --> 00:02:30.216
Super easy job. But less than
six months into that job,

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.385
he had to resign
after CNN uncovered

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:33.919
racist and homophobic comments

00:02:33.919 --> 00:02:35.421
Higbie had made
several years ago.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.056
Now where did he make
these comments?

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:39.658
Did he make them in a whispered
conversation in a crowded bar?

00:02:39.658 --> 00:02:42.028
A message board
full of fellow racists?

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:44.564
No, he made them fully
on the radio.

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.633
[ Laughter ]
Wow, not sure that's

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.568
the best way to jack up
your book sales.

00:03:22.568 --> 00:03:25.270
[ Laughter ]
"Gays, Muslims, Mexicans,

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:26.405
"and Rhode Island
can go to hell.

00:03:26.405 --> 00:03:28.474
Everyone else,
check out my new book!"

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:29.875
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:31.644
And while you're at it,
pick up Carl's other books,

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.646
"Chicken Soup for the Soulless"
and "Fifty Shades of Cray."

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:36.582
[ Laughter ]
Also --

00:03:36.582 --> 00:03:41.821
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:44.891
You know you're insane when you
go after Rhode Island.

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:46.292
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.494
"Rhode Island's been pulling the
wool over our eyes for too long.

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:51.297
Face it, you're just
Connecticut's foreskin!"

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:55.101
[ Audience groans ]

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:58.171
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:01.340
So after those comments
came out,

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.176
Higbie was fired from his job.

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:04.477
So that's the end for him,
right?

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:07.379
You can't come back from that.
Well, not exactly.

00:04:07.379 --> 00:04:09.682
-A former Navy SEAL and Trump
administration staffer who

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:14.354
resigned after racist, sexist,
homophobic remarks

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.155
that he had made on the radio
were exposed

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:19.025
has now been hired
by a pro-Trump group --

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:21.927
a pro-Trump group whose leaders
Trump had dinner with

00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:24.096
just last week.

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:26.566
-He was fired and then promptly
hired by the political Super PAC

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:27.800
that's working
with the President

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.602
which sends a message
about what they view as

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:31.170
tolerable and not tolerable.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.738
-So Higbie did something
terrible,

00:04:32.738 --> 00:04:34.373
but instead of getting rid
of him,

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:36.008
they just moved him
to a new job.

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:39.846
To put it in Catholic terms, he
got moved to another diocese.

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:41.413
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.413 --> 00:04:42.915
"This is Father Pat.

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:45.918
He just moved here
from Boston, Akron, and Omaha."

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.587
"Kids, get in the car."

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:49.354
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.354 --> 00:04:51.758
And not only was Higbie hired
by a pro-Trump group,

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:53.726
but he's still also still...

00:04:59.666 --> 00:05:03.469
So the guy who repeatedly said
racist things about black people

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:05.404
is still on the board of a group

00:05:05.404 --> 00:05:08.041
run by the National Diversity
Coalition.

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:11.010
That's like Charlie Sheen
teaching D.A.R.E.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.145
[ Laughter ]
"So remember, kids,

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:15.848
if someone offers you drugs,
you point them my way."

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:17.049
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:18.250
So despite all
of his horrible remarks,

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.385
Higbie is still working
for Trump,

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:20.453
and he's not the only one.

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:22.354
Just a few months
after Higbie resigned,

00:05:22.354 --> 00:05:24.991
Trump's personal aide,
28-year-old John McEntee,

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:27.293
was abruptly forced out as well.

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:29.595
-A personal aide
to President Trump escorted out

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:32.732
of the White House
under a cloud of controversy.

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:33.966
-Johnny McEntee,

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:36.635
President Trump's personal
assistant, his body man,

00:05:36.635 --> 00:05:38.237
abruptly forced out of his post

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:41.040
and escorted off
the White House grounds Monday.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:43.242
NBC News confirming McEntee
is under investigation

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:46.912
by the Secret Service for
serious financial crimes.

00:05:46.912 --> 00:05:49.114
McEntee's departure strips
the President of another

00:05:49.114 --> 00:05:51.817
of his closest
and longest serving aides.

00:05:51.817 --> 00:05:54.253
-Side note, buddy,
if that's your office,

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:57.123
you don't need to put on a tie.

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:59.125
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:01.694
That's like driving
the bulldozer at a landfill

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:03.362
in a top hat and tails.

00:06:03.362 --> 00:06:05.364
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.364 --> 00:06:07.900
Now an investigation found
that McEntee's gambling habits

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:10.602
had posed a security risk,
but thanks to President Trump,

00:06:10.602 --> 00:06:13.539
he was able to bounce back
almost immediately.

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:15.608
-Johnny McEntee's very much
remaining

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:17.009
in the President's orbit because

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:20.245
just minutes after this news
broke of his departure,

00:06:20.245 --> 00:06:23.382
the Trump campaign announced
that they had hired him

00:06:23.382 --> 00:06:25.351
to work as senior adviser

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:28.421
for those re-election efforts
in 2020.

00:06:28.421 --> 00:06:30.455
-So he got escorted off
the White House grounds

00:06:30.455 --> 00:06:32.692
and into a promotion.

00:06:32.692 --> 00:06:35.327
That's like getting thrown out
of a bar and the bouncer saying,

00:06:35.327 --> 00:06:36.729
"Get out and stay out

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:39.966
and come back tomorrow,
'cause you're the manager now!"

00:06:39.966 --> 00:06:43.168
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.168 --> 00:06:46.271
Trump keeps recycling
these people and others

00:06:46.271 --> 00:06:49.107
because he only uses one
yardstick to measure employees.

00:06:49.107 --> 00:06:51.877
"Are they loyal to me?"
And the problem with that is

00:06:51.877 --> 00:06:54.580
that the kinds of people who
are unquestionably loyal

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.482
to an ignorant bigot like Trump

00:06:56.482 --> 00:06:58.584
are pretty much
always terrible people.

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:01.887
There's no pool of thoughtful
and qualified candidates for him

00:07:01.887 --> 00:07:05.257
to draw from, because you can't
be thoughtful and qualified

00:07:05.257 --> 00:07:07.193
and also loyal to a President
who is neither.

00:07:07.193 --> 00:07:11.197
So despite having been fired
or having shamefully resigned

00:07:11.197 --> 00:07:12.998
because of racist comments
or straight up crimes,

00:07:12.998 --> 00:07:15.868
none of these people have really
suffered the consequences

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:19.171
you and I probably would have
had we made similar mistakes

00:07:19.171 --> 00:07:21.741
at such a high profile job,
or any job for that matter.

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:24.143
If you have an interview
at Chipotle and they say,

00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:26.679
"Why do you want to work here?"
And you say, "well, I got fired

00:07:26.679 --> 00:07:28.747
from Taco Bell for screaming
the 'N'-word,"

00:07:28.747 --> 00:07:30.283
they will not hire you.

00:07:30.283 --> 00:07:31.750
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:34.386
But I know someone who might.

00:07:34.386 --> 00:07:36.755
[ Audience groans ]
This has been "The Check In."

00:07:36.755 --> 00:07:38.657
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:38.657 --> 00:07:40.059
[ Bell dings ]

